  "summary": "Intricate embroidered border bands featuring geometric and natural motifs with spiritual significance.",
  "description": "Ikarkar bands are created using a distinctive chain stitch technique with silk or cotton thread, forming complex patterns that represent animals, plants, and spiritual concepts. These embroidered borders were traditionally applied to attush robes and other garments, serving both decorative and protective functions.",
